IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cb2-nouns`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), Part IX, sections 94 to 101 -- RECEIVERS,
-- RECEIVER-MANAGERS AND SEQUESTRATORS: what each may do, when the directors' powers cease, how each must
-- act, the court's power to give directions, and the appointee's duties. Layer 1.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Encoded from a plain-text rendering of the Justice Canada consolidation current to
-- 2026-09-30, which is not an official version; nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RULE. Named `<what it works out> within s <section>`. Where a provision says what follows in
-- a stated case, the rule is TRUE when that case holds; FALSE means only that this provision does not apply.
-- A rule whose result is a MAYBE returns NOTHING where the text is silent for the case.
-- Within this module a rule that depends on a sibling calls it and takes its inputs. A cross-reference to
-- another module is a plain input and says so ("out of range: section N (piece X)").

§ `s 94 Functions of receiver or sequestrator`

-- A receiver or sequestrator of any property of a corporation may, subject to the rights of secured
-- creditors, receive the income from the property, pay the liabilities connected with it and realize the
-- security interest of those on whose behalf they are appointed. A receiver-manager is not named, so s 94
-- gives it nothing (s 95 is its section).
-- src:1169 | Functions of receiver or sequestrator
-- src:1170 | 94 A receiver or sequestrator of any property of a corporation may, subject to the rights of secured creditors, receive the income from the property, pay the liabilities connected with the property and realize the security interest of those on behalf of whom the receiver or sequestrator is appointed, but, except to the extent permitted by a court, the receiver or sequestrator may not carry on the business of the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 94 (src:1169-1170)
GIVEN `the kind of appointee` IS A `Kind of appointee under Part IX`
      `the exercise would defeat the rights of a secured creditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the appointee may receive the income, pay the liabilities and realize the security interest within s 94` MEANS
        (   `the kind of appointee` EQUALS `a receiver appointed in respect of property of a corporation`
         OR `the kind of appointee` EQUALS `a sequestrator of property of a corporation`)
    AND (NOT `the exercise would defeat the rights of a secured creditor`)

-- "But, except to the extent permitted by a court, the receiver or sequestrator may not carry on the business
-- of the corporation." JUST FALSE: a receiver or sequestrator without a court's permission may not. JUST TRUE:
-- with the court's permission, to the extent permitted. NOTHING: a receiver-manager, which s 94 does not name.
-- src:1169 | Functions of receiver or sequestrator
-- src:1170 | 94 A receiver or sequestrator of any property of a corporation may, subject to the rights of secured creditors, receive the income from the property, pay the liabilities connected with the property and realize the security interest of those on behalf of whom the receiver or sequestrator is appointed, but, except to the extent permitted by a court, the receiver or sequestrator may not carry on the business of the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 94 (src:1169-1170)
GIVEN `the kind of appointee` IS A `Kind of appointee under Part IX`
      `a court permits the appointee to carry on the business of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the appointee may carry on the business of the corporation within s 94` MEANS
    IF     (`the kind of appointee` EQUALS `a receiver appointed in respect of property of a corporation`)
        OR (`the kind of appointee` EQUALS `a sequestrator of property of a corporation`)
    THEN JUST `a court permits the appointee to carry on the business of the corporation`
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `s 95 Functions of receiver-manager`

-- src:1171 | Functions of receiver-manager
-- src:1172 | 95 A receiver-manager of the corporation may carry on any business of the corporation to protect the security interest of those on behalf of whom the receiver-manager is appointed.
@ref CBCA s 95 (src:1171-1172)
GIVEN `the kind of appointee` IS A `Kind of appointee under Part IX`
      `the business is carried on to protect the security interest of those on behalf of whom the receiver-manager is appointed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the receiver-manager may carry on the business of the corporation within s 95` MEANS
        `the kind of appointee` EQUALS `a receiver-manager of a corporation`
    AND `the business is carried on to protect the security interest of those on behalf of whom the receiver-manager is appointed`

§ `s 96 Directors' powers cease`

-- The directors' powers that the receiver-manager or sequestrator is authorized to exercise may not be
-- exercised by the directors until the appointee is discharged. TRUE when the bar applies.
-- src:1173 | Directors’ powers cease
-- src:1174 | 96 If a receiver-manager or sequestrator is appointed by a court or under an instrument or act, the powers of the directors of the corporation that the receiver-manager or sequestrator is authorized to exercise may not be exercised by the directors until the receiver-manager or sequestrator is discharged.
@ref CBCA s 96 (src:1173-1174)
GIVEN `the kind of appointee` IS A `Kind of appointee under Part IX`
      `the appointee is authorized to exercise the power of the directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appointee has been discharged` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the directors may not exercise the power within s 96` MEANS
        (   `the kind of appointee` EQUALS `a receiver-manager of a corporation`
         OR `the kind of appointee` EQUALS `a sequestrator of property of a corporation`)
    AND `the appointee is authorized to exercise the power of the directors`
    AND (NOT `the appointee has been discharged`)

§ `s 97 Duty to act`

-- src:1175 | Duty to act
-- src:1176 | 97 A receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator appointed by a court shall act in accordance with the directions of the court.
@ref CBCA s 97 (src:1175-1176)
DECLARE `Way an appointee is appointed under Part IX` IS ONE OF
    `appointed by a court`
    `appointed under an instrument or act`

-- src:1175 | Duty to act
-- src:1176 | 97 A receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator appointed by a court shall act in accordance with the directions of the court.
@ref CBCA s 97 (src:1175-1176)
GIVEN `the way the appointee is appointed` IS A `Way an appointee is appointed under Part IX`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the appointee must act in accordance with the directions of the court within s 97` MEANS
    `the way the appointee is appointed` EQUALS `appointed by a court`

-- src:1175 | Duty to act
-- src:1176 | 97 A receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator appointed by a court shall act in accordance with the directions of the court.
@ref CBCA s 97 (src:1175-1176)
GIVEN `the way the appointee is appointed` IS A `Way an appointee is appointed under Part IX`
      `the appointee acts in accordance with the directions of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the appointee has complied with s 97` MEANS
        (NOT `the appointee must act in accordance with the directions of the court within s 97` `the way the appointee is appointed`)
    OR  `the appointee acts in accordance with the directions of the court`

§ `s 98 Duty under instrument or act`

-- src:1177 | Duty under instrument or act
-- src:1178 | 98 A receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator appointed under an instrument or act shall act in accordance with that instrument or act and any direction of a court made under section 100.
@ref CBCA s 98 (src:1177-1178)
GIVEN `the way the appointee is appointed` IS A `Way an appointee is appointed under Part IX`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the appointee must act in accordance with the instrument or act and any direction of a court within s 98` MEANS
    `the way the appointee is appointed` EQUALS `appointed under an instrument or act`

-- src:1177 | Duty under instrument or act
-- src:1178 | 98 A receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator appointed under an instrument or act shall act in accordance with that instrument or act and any direction of a court made under section 100.
@ref CBCA s 98 (src:1177-1178)
GIVEN `the way the appointee is appointed` IS A `Way an appointee is appointed under Part IX`
      `the appointee acts in accordance with the instrument or act and any direction of a court made under section 100` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the appointee has complied with s 98` MEANS
        (NOT `the appointee must act in accordance with the instrument or act and any direction of a court within s 98` `the way the appointee is appointed`)
    OR  `the appointee acts in accordance with the instrument or act and any direction of a court made under section 100`

§ `s 99 Duty of care`

-- Appointed under an instrument or act. NOTHING: the appointee was appointed by a court, so s 99 says nothing.
-- src:1179 | Duty of care
-- src:1180 | 99 A receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator of a corporation appointed under an instrument or act shall
-- src:1181 | (a) act honestly and in good faith; and
-- src:1182 | (b) deal with any property of the corporation in their possession or control in a commercially reasonable manner.
@ref CBCA s 99 (src:1179-1182)
GIVEN `the way the appointee is appointed` IS A `Way an appointee is appointed under Part IX`
      `the appointee acts honestly and in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appointee deals with any property of the corporation in their possession or control in a commercially reasonable manner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the appointee has discharged the duty of care within s 99` MEANS
    IF `the way the appointee is appointed` EQUALS `appointed under an instrument or act`
    THEN JUST (    `the appointee acts honestly and in good faith`
               AND `the appointee deals with any property of the corporation in their possession or control in a commercially reasonable manner`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `s 100 Directions given by court`

-- src:1183 | Directions given by court
-- src:1184 | 100 On an application by a receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator, whether appointed by a court or under an instrument or act, or on an application by any interested person, a court may make any order it thinks fit including, without limiting the generality of the foregoing,
@ref CBCA s 100 (src:1183-1184)
GIVEN `the applicant is a receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator, however appointed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is an interested person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a court may make any order it thinks fit within s 100` MEANS
        `the applicant is a receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator, however appointed`
    OR  `the applicant is an interested person`

-- The orders the text names, "without limiting the generality of the foregoing". NOTHING: the application is
-- not by an appointee or an interested person.
-- src:1183 | Directions given by court
-- src:1184 | 100 On an application by a receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator, whether appointed by a court or under an instrument or act, or on an application by any interested person, a court may make any order it thinks fit including, without limiting the generality of the foregoing,
-- src:1185 | (a) an order appointing, replacing or discharging a receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator and approving their accounts;
-- src:1186 | (b) an order determining the notice to be given to any person or dispensing with notice to any person;
-- src:1187 | (c) an order fixing the remuneration of the receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator;
-- src:1188 | (d) an order requiring the receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator, or a person by or on behalf of whom the receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator is appointed, to make good any default in connection with the receiver’s, receiver-manager’s or sequestrator’s custody or management of the property and business of the corporation, or to relieve any such person from any default on any terms that the court thinks fit, and to confirm any act of the receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator; and
-- src:1189 | (e) an order giving directions on any matter relating to the duties of the receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator.
@ref CBCA s 100 (src:1183-1189)
DECLARE `Order a court may make under s 100` IS ONE OF
    `an order appointing, replacing or discharging a receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator and approving their accounts`
    `an order determining the notice to be given to any person or dispensing with notice to any person`
    `an order fixing the remuneration of the receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator`
    `an order requiring the appointee, or a person by or on behalf of whom they are appointed, to make good a default, or relieving such a person from a default on terms the court thinks fit, and confirming an act of the appointee`
    `an order giving directions on any matter relating to the duties of the receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator`

-- src:1183 | Directions given by court
-- src:1184 | 100 On an application by a receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator, whether appointed by a court or under an instrument or act, or on an application by any interested person, a court may make any order it thinks fit including, without limiting the generality of the foregoing,
-- src:1185 | (a) an order appointing, replacing or discharging a receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator and approving their accounts;
-- src:1186 | (b) an order determining the notice to be given to any person or dispensing with notice to any person;
-- src:1187 | (c) an order fixing the remuneration of the receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator;
-- src:1188 | (d) an order requiring the receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator, or a person by or on behalf of whom the receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator is appointed, to make good any default in connection with the receiver’s, receiver-manager’s or sequestrator’s custody or management of the property and business of the corporation, or to relieve any such person from any default on any terms that the court thinks fit, and to confirm any act of the receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator; and
-- src:1189 | (e) an order giving directions on any matter relating to the duties of the receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator.
@ref CBCA s 100 (src:1183-1189)
GIVEN `the applicant is a receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator, however appointed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is an interested person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF `Order a court may make under s 100`)
`the orders the text names within s 100` MEANS
    IF `a court may make any order it thinks fit within s 100`
           `the applicant is a receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator, however appointed`
           `the applicant is an interested person`
    THEN JUST (LIST `an order appointing, replacing or discharging a receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator and approving their accounts`,
                    `an order determining the notice to be given to any person or dispensing with notice to any person`,
                    `an order fixing the remuneration of the receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator`,
                    `an order requiring the appointee, or a person by or on behalf of whom they are appointed, to make good a default, or relieving such a person from a default on terms the court thinks fit, and confirming an act of the appointee`,
                    `an order giving directions on any matter relating to the duties of the receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `s 101 Duties of receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator`

-- (a) "Immediately" is a judgement about timing that the caller makes: the inputs say whether the appointee
-- notified the Director immediately (fork F-P9-1).
-- src:1190 | Duties of receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator
-- src:1191 | 101 A receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator shall
-- src:1192 | (a) immediately notify the Director of their appointment and discharge;
@ref CBCA s 101(a) (src:1190-1192)
GIVEN `the appointee notified the Director immediately of their appointment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appointee has been discharged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appointee notified the Director immediately of their discharge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the appointee has notified the Director as required within s 101(a)` MEANS
        `the appointee notified the Director immediately of their appointment`
    AND (   (NOT `the appointee has been discharged`)
         OR `the appointee notified the Director immediately of their discharge`)

-- src:1190 | Duties of receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator
-- src:1191 | 101 A receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator shall
-- src:1192 | (a) immediately notify the Director of their appointment and discharge;
-- src:1193 | (b) take into their custody and control the property of the corporation in accordance with the court order or instrument or act under which they are appointed;
@ref CBCA s 101(b) (src:1190-1193)
GIVEN `the appointee has taken the property of the corporation into their custody and control in accordance with the court order or instrument or act under which they are appointed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the appointee has taken custody and control as required within s 101(b)` MEANS
    `the appointee has taken the property of the corporation into their custody and control in accordance with the court order or instrument or act under which they are appointed`

-- src:1190 | Duties of receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator
-- src:1191 | 101 A receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator shall
-- src:1192 | (a) immediately notify the Director of their appointment and discharge;
-- src:1193 | (b) take into their custody and control the property of the corporation in accordance with the court order or instrument or act under which they are appointed;
-- src:1194 | (c) open and maintain a bank account in their name as receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator of the corporation for the moneys of the corporation coming under their control;
@ref CBCA s 101(c) (src:1190-1194)
GIVEN `the appointee has opened and maintains a bank account in their name as receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator of the corporation for the moneys of the corporation coming under their control` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the appointee has opened and maintains the bank account as required within s 101(c)` MEANS
    `the appointee has opened and maintains a bank account in their name as receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator of the corporation for the moneys of the corporation coming under their control`

-- src:1190 | Duties of receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator
-- src:1191 | 101 A receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator shall
-- src:1192 | (a) immediately notify the Director of their appointment and discharge;
-- src:1193 | (b) take into their custody and control the property of the corporation in accordance with the court order or instrument or act under which they are appointed;
-- src:1194 | (c) open and maintain a bank account in their name as receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator of the corporation for the moneys of the corporation coming under their control;
-- src:1195 | (d) keep detailed accounts of all transactions carried out as receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator;
@ref CBCA s 101(d) (src:1190-1195)
GIVEN `the appointee keeps detailed accounts of all transactions carried out as receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the appointee keeps the detailed accounts as required within s 101(d)` MEANS
    `the appointee keeps detailed accounts of all transactions carried out as receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator`

-- (e) The appointee keeps accounts of their administration available during usual business hours for
-- inspection by the directors. The directors' side of the same relation is the second rule.
-- src:1190 | Duties of receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator
-- src:1191 | 101 A receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator shall
-- src:1192 | (a) immediately notify the Director of their appointment and discharge;
-- src:1193 | (b) take into their custody and control the property of the corporation in accordance with the court order or instrument or act under which they are appointed;
-- src:1194 | (c) open and maintain a bank account in their name as receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator of the corporation for the moneys of the corporation coming under their control;
-- src:1195 | (d) keep detailed accounts of all transactions carried out as receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator;
-- src:1196 | (e) keep accounts of their administration that shall be available during usual business hours for inspection by the directors of the corporation;
@ref CBCA s 101(e) (src:1190-1196)
GIVEN `the appointee keeps accounts of their administration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accounts are available during usual business hours for inspection by the directors of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the appointee makes the accounts available as required within s 101(e)` MEANS
        `the appointee keeps accounts of their administration`
    AND `the accounts are available during usual business hours for inspection by the directors of the corporation`

-- src:1190 | Duties of receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator
-- src:1191 | 101 A receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator shall
-- src:1192 | (a) immediately notify the Director of their appointment and discharge;
-- src:1193 | (b) take into their custody and control the property of the corporation in accordance with the court order or instrument or act under which they are appointed;
-- src:1194 | (c) open and maintain a bank account in their name as receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator of the corporation for the moneys of the corporation coming under their control;
-- src:1195 | (d) keep detailed accounts of all transactions carried out as receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator;
-- src:1196 | (e) keep accounts of their administration that shall be available during usual business hours for inspection by the directors of the corporation;
@ref CBCA s 101(e) (src:1190-1196)
GIVEN `the person is a director of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is during usual business hours` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a director may inspect the accounts of the administration within s 101(e)` MEANS
        `the person is a director of the corporation`
    AND `it is during usual business hours`

-- (f) At least once in every six month period after the date of the appointment, financial statements of the
-- administration, as far as practicable in the form required by section 155 (out of range: section 155
-- (piece cb3)). A six month period is complete once the day asked about is on or after the day that starts the
-- next one; every complete period must hold at least one statement.
-- src:1190 | Duties of receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator
-- src:1191 | 101 A receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator shall
-- src:1192 | (a) immediately notify the Director of their appointment and discharge;
-- src:1193 | (b) take into their custody and control the property of the corporation in accordance with the court order or instrument or act under which they are appointed;
-- src:1194 | (c) open and maintain a bank account in their name as receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator of the corporation for the moneys of the corporation coming under their control;
-- src:1195 | (d) keep detailed accounts of all transactions carried out as receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator;
-- src:1196 | (e) keep accounts of their administration that shall be available during usual business hours for inspection by the directors of the corporation;
-- src:1197 | (f) prepare at least once in every six month period after the date of their appointment financial statements of their administration as far as is practicable in the form required by section 155; and
@ref CBCA s 101(f) (src:1190-1197)
GIVEN `the date of the appointment` IS A DATE
      `the dates on which the appointee prepared financial statements of the administration` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`financial statements were prepared in each completed six month period within s 101(f)` MEANS
    `from period` 0
    WHERE
        `the start of period` k MEANS
            `the last day of` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS (6 TIMES k), `unit of time` IS `calendar months`) `counted from` `the date of the appointment`
        `from period` k MEANS
            IF `the day asked about` LESS THAN (`the start of period` (k PLUS 1))
            THEN TRUE
            ELSE     any (GIVEN d YIELD d AT LEAST (`the start of period` k) AND d LESS THAN (`the start of period` (k PLUS 1))) `the dates on which the appointee prepared financial statements of the administration`
                 AND `from period` (k PLUS 1)

-- src:1190 | Duties of receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator
-- src:1191 | 101 A receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator shall
-- src:1192 | (a) immediately notify the Director of their appointment and discharge;
-- src:1193 | (b) take into their custody and control the property of the corporation in accordance with the court order or instrument or act under which they are appointed;
-- src:1194 | (c) open and maintain a bank account in their name as receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator of the corporation for the moneys of the corporation coming under their control;
-- src:1195 | (d) keep detailed accounts of all transactions carried out as receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator;
-- src:1196 | (e) keep accounts of their administration that shall be available during usual business hours for inspection by the directors of the corporation;
-- src:1197 | (f) prepare at least once in every six month period after the date of their appointment financial statements of their administration as far as is practicable in the form required by section 155; and
@ref CBCA s 101(f) (src:1190-1197)
GIVEN `the date of the appointment` IS A DATE
      `the dates on which the appointee prepared financial statements of the administration` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
      `the statements are in the form required by section 155 as far as is practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the appointee has prepared the financial statements as required within s 101(f)` MEANS
        `financial statements were prepared in each completed six month period within s 101(f)`
            `the date of the appointment`
            `the dates on which the appointee prepared financial statements of the administration`
            `the day asked about`
    AND `the statements are in the form required by section 155 as far as is practicable`

-- (g) On completion of their duties the appointee renders a final account in the form adopted for the
-- interim accounts under (f). The duty arises on completion; it is met when the account is rendered in
-- that form.
-- src:1190 | Duties of receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator
-- src:1191 | 101 A receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator shall
-- src:1192 | (a) immediately notify the Director of their appointment and discharge;
-- src:1193 | (b) take into their custody and control the property of the corporation in accordance with the court order or instrument or act under which they are appointed;
-- src:1194 | (c) open and maintain a bank account in their name as receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator of the corporation for the moneys of the corporation coming under their control;
-- src:1195 | (d) keep detailed accounts of all transactions carried out as receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator;
-- src:1196 | (e) keep accounts of their administration that shall be available during usual business hours for inspection by the directors of the corporation;
-- src:1197 | (f) prepare at least once in every six month period after the date of their appointment financial statements of their administration as far as is practicable in the form required by section 155; and
-- src:1198 | (g) on completion of their duties, render a final account of their administration in the form adopted for interim accounts under paragraph (f).
@ref CBCA s 101(g) (src:1190-1198)
GIVEN `the appointee has completed their duties` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appointee has rendered a final account of their administration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the final account is in the form adopted for interim accounts under paragraph 101(f)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the appointee has rendered the final account as required within s 101(g)` MEANS
        (NOT `the appointee has completed their duties`)
    OR  (    `the appointee has rendered a final account of their administration`
         AND `the final account is in the form adopted for interim accounts under paragraph 101(f)`)
